Inspect a stick — partitions, filesystems, labels, vendor
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Read-only. Nothing is changed, so no command asks for confirmation and the
recipe behaves identically with -s.

WHAT FOR
  Before formatting or writing: is this really the right stick?
  After formatting: did the filesystem and label turn out as intended?
  When something is odd: why does the stick look smaller than it is?

WHAT IT SHOWS
  lsblk       device and partition tree with size, FS, label, mountpoint
  blkid       UUIDs and filesystem types of every partition
  fdisk -l    partition table type (gpt/dos) and sector boundaries
  udevadm     vendor, model, serial, bus — which stick is this?

TYPICAL FINDINGS
  "32 GB stick, but only 4 GB visible" -> an old isohybrid ISO is still on it.
  The remaining capacity sits in an unused gap -> 'usb wipe', then 'usb format'.

  "Two partitions, one tiny and vfat" -> also an ISO leftover (EFI partition).

  fdisk reports "doesn't contain a valid partition table" -> the stick is blank,
  'usb format' has not run yet.
